    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5633bfa1-b487-3538-b80a-986e3c397527",
                "word": "breadbasket",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "eac0ae00-42cb-41b2-9ea4-b7f698c03a2c",
                        "entry_id": "5633bfa1-b487-3538-b80a-986e3c397527",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "breadbaskets"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ff2ee01-4b48-3efd-9c83-d6a1b95f2e4a",
                        "entry_id": "5633bfa1-b487-3538-b80a-986e3c397527",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A basket used for storing or carrying bread."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "948e8e5b-ff2a-45c2-8906-d10a00739a7c",
                                "sense_id": "3ff2ee01-4b48-3efd-9c83-d6a1b95f2e4a",
                                "text": "In theſe eaſtern countries they eat upon the plain ground, and when it is dinner-time they ſpread a round piece of leather, and lay about it tapeſtry, and ſometimes cuſhions, whereupon they ſit croſs-leg'd before they begin to eat, […] At laſt they take up the leathern table with bread and all, which ſerveth them alſo inſtead of a table-cloth and bread-basket, they draw it together with a ſtring lik a purſe, and hang it up in the next corner."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9a0aff8-d7fc-4f61-aa12-8a5b327b3c8a",
                                "sense_id": "3ff2ee01-4b48-3efd-9c83-d6a1b95f2e4a",
                                "text": "One of the servants went to a bread-basket there, and finding the damask napkin eaten away, she was led to see if any mouse-holes were to be seen: for this purpose she removed the bread-basket, and behind it she saw a bundle of something that looked very like white cotton; she touched it, and out jumped the little dormouse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "66c67c2f-9641-4927-840c-c784b5195e71",
                                "sense_id": "3ff2ee01-4b48-3efd-9c83-d6a1b95f2e4a",
                                "text": "Everything was impeccably organized for the dinner. Platters and salad bowls, bread baskets, pumpkin pies. The oven gave off a mouthwatering smell as we sat on a couple of high stools beneath the hanging pans."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d25ac355-1174-35b1-a775-405d6d69eec9",
                        "entry_id": "5633bfa1-b487-3538-b80a-986e3c397527",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A region which has favourable conditions to produce a large quantity of grain or, by extension, other food products; a food bowl."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee488827-1c43-4fc3-bf38-ab38075f1436",
                                "sense_id": "d25ac355-1174-35b1-a775-405d6d69eec9",
                                "text": "[I]t is worth noting that if global warming produces a migration of the earth's breadbaskets, then it might damage one country's agriculture, while benefiting another's."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "236bf226-806f-4870-8c83-0a1090e00726",
                                "sense_id": "d25ac355-1174-35b1-a775-405d6d69eec9",
                                "text": "Canada at the turn of the century had become the breadbasket of the British Empire and industrialised Europe and wheat grown on the prairies was consolidated in elevator at Fort William, Ontario to await shipment overseas."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "602c9f31-55d2-33b1-ad4c-d0c0bd18cbfe",
                        "entry_id": "5633bfa1-b487-3538-b80a-986e3c397527",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The abdomen or stomach, especially as a vulnerable part of the body in an attack."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "humorous"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3cf0fbc-b909-40df-a1e7-58bb7c9210e3",
                                "sense_id": "602c9f31-55d2-33b1-ad4c-d0c0bd18cbfe",
                                "text": "Tom Oliver thought he'd a very heavy stake in this here affair, as he was to fight Shelton, on the 23d, for a hundred. […] (Give it them, Tom! hit them in the bread-basket!)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "878ff424-fd04-4fa5-b2f5-cf25d581ea2b",
                                "sense_id": "602c9f31-55d2-33b1-ad4c-d0c0bd18cbfe",
                                "text": "[S]ince you've been ill I've been eating your pork and drinking your grog, which latter can't be too plentiful in the Bay of Biscay. And now that I've cured you, you'll be tucking all that into your own little breadbasket, so that I'm no gainer, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "83e45b0f-5790-4869-8bb8-f52fa70ef668",
                        "source_entry_id": "5633bfa1-b487-3538-b80a-986e3c397527",
                        "source_sense_description": "basket for storing or carrying bread",
                        "target_lang_word": "broodmand",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "broodmand",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a839ff5-25f7-3de5-b13f-fa2cdec68d25",
                                        "entry_id": "a3929de6-742a-3961-85ae-463b93201df1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "een grote rietenmand die men gebruikt bij het bezorgen van brood"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38a2a9de-cf14-4ab9-9ac0-e229796c8143",
                                                "sense_id": "7a839ff5-25f7-3de5-b13f-fa2cdec68d25",
                                                "text": "De onteigeningen droegen ertoe bij dat Zimbabwe van de ‘broodmand’ van Afrika veranderde in een hongerend land. Volgens de Verenigde Naties zijn 7 miljoen van de 12 miljoen Zimbabweanen nu aangewezen op buitenlandse voedselhulp."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b6c2444b-a783-3b39-9966-e564b7c97f3c",
                                        "entry_id": "a3929de6-742a-3961-85ae-463b93201df1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "klein open mandje voor op tafel waarin men brood kan presenteren"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ec7c801-1090-46f3-8cb9-cc140c152618",
                                                "sense_id": "b6c2444b-a783-3b39-9966-e564b7c97f3c",
                                                "text": "De man met het windjack, eind veertig, vroeg om drie flessen rode wijn. Toen begon hij de slinger geconcentreerd om de flessen te bewegen. Na een paar seconden van intense concentratie koos hij de linkerfles uit. Daarna bewoog hij de slinger boven zijn bord, zijn bestek, zijn servet en zelfs de broodmand."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f41a30a2-8809-4b4d-8f15-4e04545bdcb7",
                        "source_entry_id": "5633bfa1-b487-3538-b80a-986e3c397527",
                        "source_sense_description": "basket for storing or carrying bread",
                        "target_lang_word": "Brotkorb",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Brotkorb",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5084587-4f9f-3bb3-99dc-f3331e4d968e",
                                        "entry_id": "9560462c-bd47-3d75-b74a-e60631613f97",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Korb, in dem Brot oder andere Backwaren aufbewahrt werden"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b7811da-0ebb-4088-8b87-ed18d3ac543d",
                                                "sense_id": "a5084587-4f9f-3bb3-99dc-f3331e4d968e",
                                                "text": "„Kannst du mir bitte den Brotkorb reichen?“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a263dee-0bd3-47f9-a0e4-50195d9d0d03",
                                                "sense_id": "a5084587-4f9f-3bb3-99dc-f3331e4d968e",
                                                "text": "„Sonja steht, von uns abgewandt, am Tisch und ist gerade dabei, Schrippen in einen großen Brotkorb zu füllen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "240c09b9-dc47-4eb8-bedb-db8c34022635",
                                                "sense_id": "a5084587-4f9f-3bb3-99dc-f3331e4d968e",
                                                "text": "„Almuth plünderte erneut den Brotkorb so gierig, als fürchte sie, zu verhungern.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "339aebdc-090e-37f4-9b99-95344b0b4f2b",
                                        "entry_id": "9560462c-bd47-3d75-b74a-e60631613f97",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Gebiet, das einen Überschuss an Lebensmitteln produziert und damit auch andere Gebiete versorgen kann"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figurative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c40fe803-0f19-4aae-99c8-e5d5a3c4eb9c",
                                                "sense_id": "339aebdc-090e-37f4-9b99-95344b0b4f2b",
                                                "text": "„2008 waren im ehemaligen Brotkorb Afrikas annähernd 5 Millionen Menschen, die Hälfte der gesamten Einwohnerzahl, dauerhaft von Lebensmittelhilfe abhängig, in deren Genuss aber nur kam, wer eine Mitgliedskarte der ZANU(PF) vorweisen konnte.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
